1.17.m:
He was banished from the kingdom by his father, being devoted to doing harm to the citizens.
His son, named Aṃśumat, was endowed with all good qualities;
he pleased his father and his father's father, the ruler of the earth.

1.19.m:
Sītāvaktra and the Sindhu went facing the west;
and toward the south went Gaṅgā, following Bhagīratha's path,
here with great velocity, there creeping slowly,
